# HAR Harness Workflow

This repository uses a `.har/` agent harness. Follow this workflow on every change.

## Before making changes

1. Read [AGENT.md](./AGENT.md) at the repo root
2. Read [.har/README.md](./.har/README.md) and [.har/stages.json](./.har/stages.json)
3. After launch, read [.har/CLAUDE.agent.md](./.har/CLAUDE.agent.md) for slot URLs and definition of done

## After making changes

Validate through the harness — do not skip verification or substitute ad-hoc npm/test commands.

### 1. HAR MCP (preferred — configured in `.cursor/mcp.json`)

- `har_launch_environment` with `agentId: 1` — once per session if not already launched
- `har_run_verification` with `agentId: 1` — fast loop (typecheck + unit tests)
- `har_run_verification` with `agentId: 1, full: true` — required before declaring work done (+ lint + build)
- `har_teardown_environment` with `agentId: 1` — cleanup when finished

### 2. HAR CLI (when `har` is installed)

```bash
har env launch 1
har env verify 1
har env verify 1 --full
har env teardown 1
```

### 3. Shell fallback (no CLI/MCP installed)

```bash
./.har/launch.sh 1
./.har/verify.sh 1
./.har/verify.sh 1 --full
./.har/teardown.sh 1
```

Work happens in an isolated git worktree by default (`~/worktrees/har_project-agent-<id>`). If your IDE workspace is the worktree, pass `--repo /path/to/main/checkout` to CLI commands; MCP is already configured with the main checkout path.

## Definition of done

- Full verification returns pass (`har env verify 1 --full`, MCP `har_run_verification` with `full: true`, or `./.har/verify.sh 1 --full`)
- New behavior has automated test coverage (typecheck, tests, lint, build)
- Do not declare work complete without running full verify
